course: dictionary
lesson: 14511
title: Words about money
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Penniless is built from two parts: penny, a small coin, and -less, which means without. Put them together and you get without any money at all.
explain: «Mia lost her purse on the bus, and by the time she got home she was penniless.» The clue is lost her purse: she had nothing left to pay with. Penniless means very poor, with no money at all.
explain: Context can also show how a character feels. «The old man sold his last chair and was penniless, but he still shared his bread with the birds.» Penniless tells you he has no money, and shared his bread shows he stayed kind even when he was poor.
fact: Penniless means having no money at all; very poor.
fact: Penny is a small coin, and -less means without, so penniless means without any pennies.
fact: Penniless is an adjective, so it describes a person: a penniless traveller.
fact: In history, many poor families were penniless in hard times.
fact: In maths, someone who spends all their money is left penniless: they have 0.
exercise: «After buying the sweets, Ali had no coins left and was penniless.» What does penniless mean? | Having a big bag of gold coins | Very rich and happy | *Having no money at all | Hungry and tired
exercise: Lily says penniless means full of pennies. What does it really mean? | *Having no money at all | Hungry for food | Lucky with coins | Full of pennies to spend
exercise: «He spent every last coin on the bus trip, and now he is penniless.» Which clue shows he has no money left? | On the bus trip | He is | *Spent every last coin | Now
test: After paying for everything, Ben has 0 pounds left. What is he? | Hungry | Lucky | *Penniless | Wealthy
test: Which sentence uses penniless correctly? | The penniless girl bought a big house with her savings. | The penniless sun shone brightly on the hill. | Penniless is a kind of fruit. | *The penniless girl had no coins for the bus.
exam: Mrs Patel was penniless after the flood. Which word means the opposite of penniless? | Poor | Lost | Tired | *Rich
